  transparency: ["Voters are demanding greater transparency in political funding.", "transparent (adj).", "Los votantes exigen una mayor transparencia en la financiación política."],

  /* ===== VOCABULARIO DE NEGACIÓN ===== */
  "by no means": ["This is by no means a comprehensive account of all the evidence.", "Seguido de inversión al inicio de frase: By no means IS this...", "Esto no es de ninguna manera un relato exhaustivo de toda la evidencia."],
  "in no way": ["This finding is in no way conclusive.", "in no way = de ninguna manera.", "Este hallazgo no es de ninguna manera concluyente."],
  "on no account": ["On no account should the details be shared before publication.", "Inversión obligatoria: On no account SHOULD...", "En ningún caso deberían compartirse los detalles antes de la publicación."],
  "under no circumstances": ["Under no circumstances are visitors permitted in the laboratory.", "Inversión obligatoria al inicio de frase.", "Bajo ninguna circunstancia se permite la entrada de visitantes al laboratorio."],
  "at no point": ["At no point during the investigation were these facts disclosed.", "Inversión: At no point DID they disclose...", "En ningún momento de la investigación se revelaron estos hechos."],
  "to no avail": ["She called for help repeatedly, but to no avail.", "= without success.", "Pidió ayuda repetidamente, pero en vano."],
  "let alone": ["The office lacks basic supplies, let alone modern equipment.", "= and even less, much less.", "La oficina carece de suministros básicos, por no hablar de equipos modernos."],
  "nothing short of": ["The speed of the response was nothing short of remarkable.", "= truly, genuinely (emphatic).", "La velocidad de la respuesta fue verdaderamente notable."],
  "anything but": ["The transition was anything but smooth.", "= the opposite of, not at all.", "La transición no fue ni mucho menos fluida."],
  "far from": ["The results were far from satisfactory.", "far from + adj/noun = not at all.", "Los resultados estaban lejos de ser satisfactorios."],

  /* ===== EXPRESIONES DE GRADO Y CANTIDAD ===== */
  "a great deal of": ["A great deal of research still needs to be done.", "= a large amount of (with uncountable nouns).", "Todavía queda mucha investigación por hacer."],
  "a wide range of": ["The report covers a wide range of topics.", "= many different types.", "El informe abarca una amplia gama de temas."],
  "a host of": ["The policy has attracted a host of critics.", "= a large number of.", "La política ha atraído a un gran número de críticos."],
  "a handful of": ["Only a handful of participants completed the full study.", "= a small number, very few.", "Solo un puñado de participantes completó el estudio completo."],
  "the vast majority of": ["The vast majority of respondents supported the change.", "= nearly all.", "La gran mayoría de los encuestados apoyó el cambio."],
  "to a great extent": ["The crisis was, to a great extent, caused by regulatory failure.", "= largely, in large measure.", "La crisis fue, en gran medida, causada por un fallo regulatorio."],
  "to some extent": ["To some extent, the criticism is fair.", "= partly, in some ways.", "En cierta medida, la crítica es justa."],
  "by far": ["This is by far the most compelling argument in the paper.", "= by a large margin.", "Este es con mucho el argumento más convincente del artículo."],
  overwhelmingly: ["The proposal was overwhelmingly rejected by the committee.", "= by a very large majority.", "La propuesta fue rechazada abrumadoramente por el comité."],
  disproportionately: ["The cuts fell disproportionately on lower-income households.", "= in a way that is too large or too small compared to what is fair.", "Los recortes recayeron de forma desproporcionada en los hogares de menores ingresos."],
  exponentially: ["The cost of the project grew exponentially.", "= at an increasingly rapid rate.", "El coste del proyecto creció exponencialmente."],
  marginally: ["The second candidate scored only marginally better than the first.", "= very slightly.", "El segundo candidato obtuvo solo marginalmente mejores resultados que el primero."],
  "precious few": ["There are precious few examples of this approach succeeding.", "= very few indeed (emphatic).", "Hay poquísimos ejemplos de que este enfoque haya tenido éxito."],

