  vicinity: ["There are no pharmacies in the vicinity of the campus.", "in the vicinity of también = approximately: in the vicinity of 500 pounds.", "No hay farmacias en las inmediaciones del campus."],
  reliable: ["The data come from a reliable source.", "reliable = fiable; reliability (n.); rely on (phrasal).", "Los datos proceden de una fuente fiable."],
  daunting: ["Writing a thesis can be daunting at first.", "a daunting task/prospect/challenge. Sinónimo: intimidating, overwhelming.", "Escribir una tesis puede resultar intimidante al principio."],
  "see fit to": ["Parliament saw fit to enact the reform without consultation.", "see fit to + infinitive = juzgar oportuno; tono formal, a menudo crítico o irónico.", "El Parlamento consideró oportuno promulgar la reforma sin consulta previa."],
  succeeding: ["In the succeeding years, the policy was quietly dropped.", "succeeding (adj.) = following, subsequent; NO confundir con succeed (v.) = tener éxito.", "En los años siguientes, la política fue silenciosamente abandonada."],
  supply: ["The supply of housing has not kept pace with demand.", "supply and demand; supply sth TO sb (v.); supplies (pl.) = suministros.", "La oferta de vivienda no ha seguido el ritmo de la demanda."],
  arise: ["Several questions arose during the seminar.", "Intransitivo: arise FROM sth = surgir de algo. NUNCA arise a problem.", "Durante el seminario surgieron varias preguntas."],
  "lead to": ["Poor sampling leads to unreliable conclusions.", "lead TO + noun/gerund; sinónimos: result in, give rise to, bring about.", "Un muestreo deficiente lleva a conclusiones poco fiables."],
  retrace: ["She retraced her steps to find the missing key.", "retrace one's steps = desandar lo andado; retrace a route = reconstruirlo.", "Deshizo sus pasos para encontrar la llave perdida."],
  regress: ["Without practice, your speaking will regress.", "Connotación negativa: implica volver a un estado peor. regression (n.).", "Sin práctica, tu expresión oral retrocederá."],
  return: ["He returned to Madrid in June after a year abroad.", "return = volver/devolver (neutro); cf. retrace (desandar), regress (retroceder).", "Regresó a Madrid en junio tras un año en el extranjero."],

